    "updated_at": "2022-03-17T11:52:51Z",
    "body": "The symbol is a regular Unicode character ([`1F17A NEGATIVE SQUARED LATIN CAPITAL LETTER K`](https://util.unicode.org/UnicodeJsps/character.jsp?a=1F17A)). I assume you'll need to install a font that provides it (I don't have a Linux system at hand right now to find out which - maybe one of the noto fonts?).\r\n\r\nThe character shouldn't be all that uncommon, but if it turns out that fonts don't regularly provide it, we'll need to consider replacing it.",
