    "updated_at": "2022-03-17T15:35:42Z",
    "body": "@davidkna `fc-list` on my system tells me that (of the things I have installed) only Symbola provides that glyph, which is somewhat surprising because it entered Unicode in 2010. Neither the Noto emoji nor the twoemoji fonts provide it.\r\n\r\nFurther poking around shows that the Noto CJK fonts provide it, as do the Noto Symbols series, but it is not an emoji.",
